# Line endings, decided once instead of per file.
#
# Git stores LF and checks out CRLF, which is what every editor pointed at this
# project already writes. Without this the repository keeps whatever each file
# happened to be saved as -- and it was genuinely mixed, some files CRLF, some
# LF, some mixed within themselves -- so the moment an editor rewrote one on
# save, a ten-line change arrived as a thousand-line diff with the real edit
# buried in it. That happened, which is why this file exists.
#
# CRLF rather than native because everything here is Windows: MSVC, Win32, WGL
# and a .cmd to build it. A deterministic answer is worth more than a portable
# one for a project that only has one platform to be portable to.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Never touched, whatever the extension heuristics think.
*.png binary
*.mp4 binary
*.jar binary
